  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Our class is on a bus. It is a big yellow bus. Teacher Kim counts the children. \"One, two, three, four.\" \"Five, six, seven, eight.\" \"Eight children!\" \"Where do we go?\" asks Leo. \"To the beach!\" says Teacher Kim. \"Hooray!\"",
      "We see the sea. The sand is white. Mia sees a bird. \"Look, a bee!\" says Leo. \"Is it a bird?\" \"No, it is not,\" says Mia. \"It is a small bee.\" Leo says, \"Wow!\" May has shells. \"Count them, Leo.\" \"One, two, three, four, five, six, seven!\" \"Seven shells!\"",
      "Teacher Kim says, \"Come here.\" \"Come to the bus, please.\" \"Bye, sea!\" says May. \"Bye, sand!\" says Leo. Teacher Kim counts again. \"Eight children!\" We are happy."
    ],
